{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>Seven days you shall offer an offering made by fire.</b> And if it is not equivalent to [the phrase] 'offering made by fire' [in] the festival of Passover:" "<b>It is a solemn assembly [atzeret].</b> Some say its meaning is 'assembly,' like the meaning of 'the assembly of traitors' [עצרת בוגדים], and the explanation is the gathering of all Israel for the three pilgrimage festivals. But they have not spoken correctly, for it is written concerning Passover, 'and on the seventh day [is] a solemn assembly [atzeret],' and it is written, 'and you shall turn in the morning and go to your tents' [Deuteronomy 16:7]. The closer [explanation] is that it is as though one is detained [נעצר] before HaShem, being freed from all worldly affairs, and the meaning of atzeret is 'you shall do no manner of labor.' And so it is written, 'at the solemn assembly [atzeret] of the festival of Passover.' [n: Ibn Ezra's biblical quotations are woven into his syntax without quotation marks in the Hebrew; I have inserted bracketed citations only where he quotes by formula 'it is written.' The expression כל מלאכת עבודה לא תעשו is itself a partial biblical quotation from the verse's own context (v. 25), quoted as a gloss on atzeret.]"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:03.605389163Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}